NAME
    test_dma - Performance DMA test

SYNOPSIS
    test_dma [--hbm] [--l3] [--addr <address>] [--no-integrity-check]
             [--loop <loop_count>] [-hv] <dev_id> <size>

DESCRIPTION
    Perform the DMA copy-in/copy-out test. The basic test process is DMA <size> bytes from
    cpu memory A into XPU memory B and then back into cpu memory C. DMA speed will be
    recored and integrity check is performed if --no-integrity-check option is not set.
    This whole process will be executed in <loop_count> interations.

OPTIONS
    --addr <address>  Specify the address of XPU memory B, if this option is not provided,
                      memory B will be malloced on given test memory type.

    --hbm  Set test memory type to HBM. If --addr is provided, this is ignored. If neither 
           --hbm nor --l3 is set, use HBM as the default type.

    --l3  Set test memory type to L3. If --addr is provided, this is ignored.

    --no-integrity-check  Do no integrity check and move to next test iteration quickly.

    --loop <loop_count>  Do <loop_count> iteration of DMA test in total, 1 if not set.

    --value <value>  Content value, 0xA or 0x5...

    --transparent-hugepage <1|0>  Use transparent hugepage to allocate continuous chunks of
                                  memory when possible, default is 1.

    --host-register <1|0> Register host memory that is page-locked and accessible to the device,
                                  default is 1.

    --host-alloc <1|0> Malloc host memory that is page-locked and accessible to the device,
                                  default is 0.
                       Under this mode, host-register and transparent-hugepage is unavailable.

    --kind <ALL|H2D|D2H> Specifies the direction of data copy,
                                  default is ALL.
                          ALL : Both host to device and device to host.
                          H2D : Host to device only.
                          D2H : Device to host only.

    -v  Print verbose information.

    -h  Print this message
